					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/experiment-log-t-92563-oc5032</guid>
				<title>Experiment-Log-T-92563-OC5032</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/experiment-log-t-92563-oc5032</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Test Log -T-92563-OC5032&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-SCP Termination Testing for SCP-5942&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the highly aggressive, unpredictable, and intelligent nature of SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
, termination testing has been ordered, with clearance from O5 Command. With major concerns raised about possible developed immunities (due to the failure of SCP-409) and other possible immunity, all tests must first be carried out on tissue and/or scale samples taken from SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
unless it is non-anomalous objects, if done with non-anomalous objects on tissue SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
can still gain Immunity. This step may be bypassed only by O5 Command order.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-890061-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-063&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Sample eradicated. Little to No traces above molecular level remain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-063 was refitted to the end of a robots arm, which was deployed into 5942&#039;s enclosure, during that time SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
was scarred and had some exposed tissues. Initial approach failed, the damage done to SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
&#039;s body before regeneration overtakes the destruction process. Newly regrown scales are not vulnerable to SCP-063&#039;s eradication effect: 5942&lt;br /&gt;
destroys the deployment arm and 063 digs a hole through the enclosure&#039;s ground, where it is later recovered. 5942&lt;br /&gt;
succeeds in extending digging through the hole and maiming 9 security personnel before containment is reestablished.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hypothesis:&lt;/strong&gt;82 is not bound to base Earth biological chemistry and it&#039;s scales are &#039;inorganic&#039;. Some of the D-class were arguing whether to even call it a &#039;living&#039; creature, at least as we understand life. This worries me, because an unliving, undying intelligent monster that can control the planet and solar system… well, that&#039;s a &lt;strong&gt;XK&lt;/strong&gt; class extinction event waiting to happen. -Agent ██████&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-173&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A, overridden by O5-Command&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-173 introduced into the containment area of SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
. SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
makes screeches several times, and tries to kill SCP-173 and blasted SCP-173&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: After review, it appears SCP-173 was unable to do lethal damage to SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
due to a major difference in physical size. A possible repeat of this test may be made if SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
was damaged enough to reduce its physical mass to a level equal with SCP-173.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; Send SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
to space in a shuttle and crash it into the ground&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5-██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Testing denied by O5-██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: Seriously? I mean… seriously? Put it in a shuttle then crash the space shuttle in to the ground with it inside… who in the [DATA EXPUNGED]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; █████W ██████████ cutting laser&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A, overridden by O5-Command&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
was unaffected by the laser even when it was pointed at its eye.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; 150&amp;#160;MT thermonuclear bomb&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Testing deneid by O5-█&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Testing denied by O5-█&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: Really? The US military did that when it was discovered, and what did they do&lt;br /&gt;
make it 30 meters taller! and do you thing this one will be any different? Yes, it&#039;s a&lt;br /&gt;
goddamn nuke, but that thing survived one before at Bikini Atoll.. O5-█&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-096&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Containment tank containing SCP-096 was placed in SCP-682&#039;s cell. Personnel vacated vicinity and the tank was opened remotely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Screams of the two entities continue for thirty-six (36) hours, at which point the noise abruptly stops. Sonar-based video feeds reveal SCP-096 severely &amp;quot;wounded&amp;quot; and huddled in the north west corner, apparently upset. Feed shows SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
on the east end of the room, approximately 2% of its initial mass absent. Re-containment teams retrieve both 096 with relative ease, but SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
resisted until it was recontained.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Further attempts to expose SCP-096 to SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
cause it to turn away from 5942, jumping in place while clawing at its face and screaming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; Space&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5-█&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5-█&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; VX gas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A, overridden by O5-Command&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5942&#039;s exposure to VX gas resulted in it coughing for about 1 hour then&lt;br /&gt;
5942 dropped to the ground coughing out a green liquid later i identified as SCP-5942&#039;s &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;blood&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
After 3 hours of coughing blood SCP-5942 regurgitated what looked like meat covered in 5942&#039;s blood. After 5 hours from initial exposure SCP-5942&#039;s scales and tissue fell off its body and was replaced with more tissue and scales. After 8 hours SCP-5942&#039;s scales and tissue stopped to fall of and 5942 began to have seizures and continued coughing blood.After 13 hours since exposed SCP-5942 began regeneration&amp;#8230;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;further attempts to expose SCP-5942 to VX gas has proven unsuccessful&lt;br /&gt;
as SCP-5942 has gained &amp;quot;immunity&amp;quot; to VX gas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note:So he is vulnerable to toxins huh&amp;#8230; then why don&#039;t we just make a &amp;quot;super toxin&amp;quot; to kill it?&lt;br /&gt;
it just gained immunity from the most dangerous toxin and the second most dangerous toxin in the world! why shouldn&#039;t we do it? No, its a waste of resources. but we still can get a big reward (SCP-5942&#039;s death). Still its not worth the risk plus a few guys think it can &amp;quot;defeat&amp;quot; the SCP-5942 Scarlet King. - Dr. ██████ and Agent █████&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-053&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A, overridden by O5-Command&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-053 introduced to SCP-5942 old containment area. SCP-5942 doesn&#039;t seem care about SCP-053&#039;s presence and just lies on the floor then says get out, and shows no sign of being affected by SCP-053. SCP-053 appears to be afraid of SCP-5942, and hides behind sandbags left in 5942&#039;s old containment area. SCP-053 approaches SCP-5942, and after several seconds of hesitation, briefly touches SCP-5942before rapidly returning to her hiding place. SCP-5942 does not react in any way and just moves its head to the right. SCP-053 approaches SCP-682 and pats its head, causing it to exhale through its forward nostrils. SCP-053 claps and hops in place several times before embracing the head of SCP-5942. For the remainder of the testing period, SCP-5942 appears to be in a very docile state, with no escape attempts being made. SCP-053 is observed to bring toys and other items to SCP-5942, and makes several drawings on its scales with crayons.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; One ordinary human child&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Child began to scream and cry when SCP-5942 was introduced into the cell. Subject was immediately swiped across the old containment area by SCP-5942.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: Okay, so that didn&#039;t work so well. Maybe the fact that the kid was crying made 5942 perceive it as hostile intent… Guest Researcher Dr. Henry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; two ordinary human childreen, drugged to cancel extreme emotional reaction&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Children stood and smiled, giggling at SCP-5942 with no sign of fear. SCP-5942 devoured the subject messily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: Hmmm… maybe we can try that again. I&#039;m sure somewhere out there there&#039;s a kid who&#039;ll make friends with it like SCP-053 did with 5942 and 682… Guest Researcher Dr. Henry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; Guest Researcher Dr. Henry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Subject screamed in terror and pounded on the door to the test facility, begging to be let out. SCP-5942 let out a Atomic ray three minutes after being introduced, 4 minutes after being introduced, Dr. Henry was eaten by 5942.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: Fing sadistic goddam asshole. I&#039;ve got no sympathy for that imbecile whatsoever. Introducing children to this fing monster? What the hell… Assistant Director Clef&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-682&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5-██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5-██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-999&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
